     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 puls per dose. At this dose, the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis goes up, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** If so, tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note saying you've verified the dose. Tell me how you'd like to proceed."
      }
     ],
